[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/ring_buffer/lib/ring_buffer.py: Author concrete RingBuffer interface: @data_type BufferError/BufferEmptyError deriving from PretenseSpecificationError, @poly_type Protocol with capacity/size/is_empty/is_full properties and operation stubs (push, pop, clear, @test_only snapshot_items); use package-qualified pretense import.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/ring_buffer/lib/ring_buffer_impl.py: Implement RingBuffer singleton on collections.deque(maxlen=10): capacity/size/is_empty/is_full accessors, push with overwrite eviction returning evicted oldest item or None, pop raising BufferEmptyError when empty, clear emptying buffer, and @test_only snapshot_items returning FIFO list copy.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/ring_buffer/pretense/ring_buffer_pretense.py: Modeled RingBuffer as a bounded FIFO model state (capacity=10 + ordered items) with 1:1 transitions for push (incl. overwrite eviction), pop (empty precondition via require), clear, snapshot_items, and capacity/size/is_empty/is_full property transitions pivoting through make_return_value; synthesized FakeRingBuffer with factory and a fixed TestRingBufferFake suite covering all 8 transitions plus FakeRingBufferFuzzTest hypothesis fuzzing.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/ring_buffer/pretense/ring_buffer_impl_pretense.py: Added RingBufferImplPseudoStateMachine inheriting the interface RingBufferStateMachine (no new state dataclass, no require_arg/Domain imports) overriding all 8 transitions with call_target pivots on the real singleton SUT plus SUT-relative postcondition observations; added TestRingBufferImplReal scenario suite (blank state, FIFO push/pop/clear, saturation eviction) and RingBufferFuzzTest hypothesis stateful fuzzing against the real SUT.
[AUDIT] benchmark_2/parts/ring_buffer/lib/ring_buffer_impl.py: PRETENSE_QA_AUDIT
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/ring_buffer/pretense/ring_buffer_impl_pretense.py: [slug:ring_buffer.pop.empty_buffer] [viol:pret_cov.transition_frequency_starvation] Facet: empty-buffer pop contracted error path Witness: buffer_size=0 exercised_pop_on_empty=0 expected_error=BufferEmptyError. The fixed scenario suite establishes coverage only for pop on a non-empty buffer; the contracted precondition ring_buffer.pop.empty_buffer (WHEN size equals zero, MUST raise BufferEmptyError) has no deterministic transition sequence in the implementation scenario tests, so the contracted error branch of pop is never driven.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/ring_buffer/pretense/ring_buffer_impl_pretense.py: Covered the contracted empty-buffer pop failure branch: added deterministic TestRingBufferImplReal.test_real_pop_on_empty_buffer_reports_empty_failure which drives push+pop back to size zero through self.checked transitions, then invokes checked pop on the empty buffer and verifies the contracted BufferEmptyError; also restored the verified module body so no specification-slug text remains in comments. Audited remaining transitions (push, clear, snapshot_items, and all properties) and confirmed pop is the only contracted error branch.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/ring_buffer/pretense/ring_buffer_pretense.py: [slug:ring_buffer.pop.empty_buffer] [viol:pret_qa.uncontracted_state_rule] Facet: empty-buffer pop state gate Witness: size=0, expected=BufferEmptyError, observed=PretenseSpecificationError. The pop transition's require(len(self.state.items) > 0) guard rejects the empty-buffer state that the low-level RingBuffer contract explicitly obligates, so the contracted BufferEmptyError on a zero-size pop can never be exercised and the model raises PretenseSpecificationError instead. The CHANGE entry that models the empty case as an 'empty precondition via require' is itself the defect: the specification states WHEN size equals zero pop MUST raise BufferEmptyError, an outcome obligation of the operation, not a call precondition that forbids the modeled empty state. Remove the blanket non-empty require gate so the zero-size pop path is representable and the contracted BufferEmptyError outcome can be observed.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/ring_buffer/pretense/ring_buffer_pretense.py: Modeled the zero-size pop failure as an operation outcome obligation instead of a caller precondition: removed the blanket non-empty require gate from the pop transition so the empty state is representable, and declared the contracted BufferEmptyError around the pivot via with raises(BufferEmptyError); the synthesized blank fake now raises the contracted error on an empty pop. Added deterministic TestRingBufferFake coverage for pop on a blank fake asserting the contracted failure and unchanged zero size. Audited sibling transitions (push, clear, snapshot_items, capacity/size/is_empty/is_full) and confirmed none declares a contracted error outcome, so no other gate needed removal.
